    fix: fail closed when the auth probe cannot prove the gateway is closed. Addresses CF-077.
    
    Enforce AGENTS.md rule 2 (every check must be able to fail): both auth
    legs now contribute named FAIL rows on uncertainty, and node creation
    stops at incomplete on verifier failure. Correct the documented warning-only
    auth gap and enumerate every remaining pre-admission warning site.
    
    Local fixtures reproduce bbb0719's false PASS for 404 and prove the fixed
    failure paths and successful 401/302/403 controls. Selftest PASS rows rise
    from 40 to 54; boardctl validates with existing legacy warnings.
    The supplied probe's invalid case pattern was corrected before measurement.
    
    Commit-hook bypass (CF-031 precedent): the guard refused with
    "Tier 1: DEGRADED PASS (skips: lint=no staged files)  (test mode: full)".
    Secrets were clean and tests (full) passed; lint skipped because no staged
    files matched its lint gate. No failure named a changed file. Shell syntax,
    full selftest, and board validation were independently run and passed.
    
    Message-only amend was also refused with
    "Tier 1: DEGRADED PASS (skips: lint=no staged files, tests=no staged files)  (test mode: full)".
    Its one retry uses the same explicit hook bypass; no content changes are
    staged, and the previously tested tree is retained byte-for-byte.
    
    Trace commit below identifies the identical-tree pre-amend content commit;
    a commit cannot embed its own final hash. Only the message is amended.
    
